ds and investment, I move my possessions, set up a small lair, and shed the vitae to hide it, twist it, and make it a suitable nightmare churn-funnel so that Yusuf feels confident he would hear distant screams and not the sounds of approach...","project_3_cast":"Me","project_3_merits":"Safe Place 1","project_4_action":"misc","project_4_title":"\"MMN Sees\"","project_4_outcome":"Maintain Mystery Cult status","project_4_description":"This is the required DT action to keep the whole Mystery Cult apparatus going. Mainting networks, grooming new members, allocating resources, solving the odd mortal cult issue. I am supporting the Mammons cult activities in the SHORE","project_4_pool_expr":"Msytery Cult Initiate 5","project_4_pool2_expr":"Presence 4 + Empathy 4","project_4_cast":"ME","sphere_1_merit":"Allies 3 (Finance)","sphere_1_action":"ambience_increase","sphere_1_outcome":"Increase the SHORE ambience","sphere_1_description":"The Mammon cult may not be good for elite members, but on their climb up its ranks the entropy of their climb maketh the garden more verdant for all kindred...","sphere_2_merit":"Allies 2 (Politics)","sphere_2_action":"ambience_increase","sphere_2_outcome":"INCREASE the HARBOUR ambience","sphere_2_description":"The subtle pro-kindred enshittification of Sydney Harbour after dark. (For the Nos 3am vibe baby!!!)The territory will be both better (for all) and worse (for mortals) in a clever way. Events will simultaneously draw people into the Harbour district, but stupid track-works close down public transport just as events let out forcing walks home. Public works for safety that actually break existing lighting. Energy saving initatives means that there is dim-lights but far apart. cost savings. it is almost like the bad ideas are deliberate....","sphere_3_merit":"Mystery Cult Initiate","sphere_3_action":"acquisition","sphere_3_outcome":"Reserve/Block access to chunks of sewer/rail networks","sphere_3_description":"The network of influence in Politics and Finance that is the MMN cult reaps its rewards in greased palms. The right bribe, the right contract, the right environmental report. Volia - whole chunks of subterranean tunnels sealed off with special works here - accidental concrete spill there, sealed off for the M11 tunnel. Tunnels, mostly bare, ugly, damp, infested. But directly underneath and nowhere all at once! It is a patchwork of forgotten RTA service tunnels, WW2 shuttered ammunition tunnels, redundant storm-water catchment sumps, etc... It is not ownership per se. It is sealing the entry points off little clusters and burying them administratively so they are nobody's business.","contact_1_request":"Contact Type: STREET\nSupporting Info: rumours of a vigiliantee in the Harbour\nRequest: The word on the street is Ballsack is rolling in the lower tiers as a vigilantee. I want details. Is this some kind of Punisher style murderer using vigilantism as a justification to kill or is there a daredevil style hand targeting the previously untouchables? The street contacts may have anecdotes and better rumours. What is his caper? I am trying to find out the why more than the what.","contact_2_request":"Contact Type: LEGAL\nSupporting Info: Previous DT searches in Finince Sphere\nRequest: Last months search indicated that there is another player with established Allies Finance in the game. A inquiry/ exposé on multi-nationals will be a good chance to look into new players in detail. (Avoid Reed Justice)","contact_3_request":"Contact Type: UNDERWORLD\nSupporting Info: whos fucking with the Harbour\nRequest: Who is dedicating any efforts to systematically messing with Harbour infrastrucure","xp_spend":"XP Claimed: 3\nTotal XP Spent: 3\nProject 1: 3XP","lore_request":"GROW action and requirements. how that interacts with territory. which territories have which social groups as focused isn't super clear how that all works. Do I need to be regent of the Shore to scramble for Allies 5? Can the regent of the shore strip that?","vamping":"yes.The surveillance cameras I am trying to procure are a gift for Conrad Sunderland. I will pass them on with the full chain-of-custody documentation that certifies they are not manipulated or modified in any way between the Israeli manufacturer and his secured delivery. It is up to his discretion whether to trust that - but I have not manipulated the cameras in any way. I make it very clear that these cameras are a gift, without strings or obligation attached and he is free to use them however he likes but he must note that there are 2 monitor portals for the cameras (there are 3 cams) and I have the second one. In the spirit of \"a pleasure shared is a pleasure doubled\". I will contact the player IC on Discord with my \"attempt\". I guess rolls will determine if it came off to secure them...\n\nMy nights are focused with either managing the cult of Mammons activities, which I see like a job taking several half nights every week. This occurs in the Shore. One of those, I will stop by the Crone Temple on night of service - explaining that the Mother offered invite that I have spontaneously accepted. (all true except the spontaneous part). This attendance is lip service to my Hostesses in the Shore. My initial actual curiosity in the sermon is minimal. But I have never actually witnessed any REAL CRUAC up close before and it might just be a surprise awakening. I should let Mother Crone Anichka roll against my Resolve+BP probably to see how compelling her sermon is. ;)\n\nI like to inhabit the Harbour now. I like it neglected to be honest and I want to savour the shittyness before the kindred money moves in. I supplemnent herd feeding there. I lurk and menace. I want the sewers (only) to be a place of twisted vibes. particularly the near the manholes, drains and rail maintenance tunnels adjacent to my Safe Place. I want everything to avoid those corners except the cockies.\n\nThis serves the long-term goal to establish a SafePlace/Warren/Necropolis for the Nos.\n[!!!] Im not going for any mechanical benefit from Nos rulebook. My XP is pre-spent in my head for the next 2 years... lol. At most I am trying to build up my own Clan status, by embodying peak-Nos'ness, supporting other clanspeeps, and reaching out along Nos lines so that the other Nos know the I/WE ARE here, lurking too. I'd be cool if we share SafePlace merits together, and my OBS5 Oubliette can make for a truly BIZONKERS commons. I reckon its narratively cool and want to try to get traction next game... I hope the STs agree?","form_feedback":"it would be cool if you had, like, a dedicated website or something, .... Should only take a couple of days.... week tops! ;)"},"updated_at":"2026-04-16T20:45:07.582Z","feeding_review":{"pool_player":"Presence 4 + Empathy 3 + Spec: Motives 1 = 12","pool_validated":"Presence 4 + Empathy 4 = 8","pool_status":"validated","notes_thread":[{"author_id":"694104767298797618","author_name":"Angelus","text":"Actual dice pool is 8, not 12 as submitted. Feedback: DP needs clarification","created_at":"2026-04-12T11:11:34.788Z"}],"story_context":"","nine_again":true,"active_feed_specs":["Motives"],"pool_mod_spec":1,"name":"","description":"I like the homeless people. The cold, dark and rains drive them into the corners where this crawler creeps. Face-in-the-crowd Yusuf blends in. He likes the dirt and the smell. \nHe likes the taste, a goon-bag of wine and a blanket are gifts enough. They sit and talk about their shit lives. Yusufs life was probably shitter, but at least they feel it, Yusuf thinks. And he tastes the goon-bag and hardship in them equally. He drinks at the end of the bin-fire in the hours just before dawn - never killing these.... no never killing. This is an act of sharing in my mind... lol\n\n*Normally* he eats from his HERD of Bankers and the Elites from behind the Mammon throne. Expensive cologne, pressed shirts. They offer their necks up - ecstatic and trembling.\n\nIt is a bland feast and sometime you just need \"home*less-cooking\".","blood_type":"Human","bonuses":"","eight_again":false,"pool_validated_by":"Angelus","pool_committed_by":"Angelus"},"projects_resolved":[{"action_type":"xp_spend","pool":null,"roll":null,"st_note":"","pool_player":"Automatic","pool_validated":"","pool_status":"no_roll","notes_thread":[{"author_id":"977695064392343652","author_name":"alchymiste","text":"This should work, no roll needed.","created_at":"2026-04-16T05:29:59.509Z"}],"story_context":"","resolved_at":null,"pool_validated_by":"Angelus"},{"action_type":"ambience_increase","pool":null,"roll":{"dice_string":"[0>6,7,9>7,9>5,4,9>1,3,9>5,7,0>9>5,6,5,1,5]","successes":7,"exceptional":true,"rolled_at":"2026-04-13T13:52:53.214Z","params":{"size":14,"again":9,"success":8,"exc":5,"rote":false}},"st_note":"","pool_player":"Presence 4 + Intimidation 4 + Spec(Veiled threat) 1 + Air of Menace 2 + Nightmare 4 = 15","pool_validated":"Presence 4 + Intimidation 5 + Nightmare 5 = 14","pool_status":"validated","notes_thread":[{"author_id":"694104767298797618","author_name":"Angelus","text":"Side effect: scares homeless out of sewers into the open air.","created_at":"2026-04-13T07:25:14.784Z"}],"story_context":"","resolved_at":null,"active_feed_specs":["Direct Threats"],"pool_mod_spec":1,"pool_mod_equipment":0,"nine_again":true,"rote":false,"eight_again":false,"st_response":"You go into the tunnels wearing a high-vis vest and a hardhat and come out wearing neither. In between, you walk every accessible passage beneath the Harbour district: storm drains, disused rail maintenance corridors, cable runs dating back to the 1930s that no longer appear on any current map. The Cave Clan have been using a junction chamber beneath Hickson Road as a base camp for years. By the end of your first night down there, they have abandoned it so completely that they leave behind two camping chairs and a battery lantern still switched on.\n\nIt is not subtle work. You move through the tunnels over the course of a week and everything that lives down there, human or otherwise, decides independently and with considerable urgency to be somewhere else. A Reddit thread appears in r/sydney titled \"anyone else getting weird vibes under Barangaroo?\" with fourteen comments and no coherent answers. Council receives three separate requests for emergency works on storm drain access points, all citing safety concerns that the callers struggle to articulate. The paperwork moves quickly. Grates get welded. Access hatches get new locks. The tunnels empty out, and what fills the silence afterwards is the particular stillness of a space that now belongs to something the previous occupants could smell but never quite see.","response_author":"a_morningstar","response_status":"draft","response_reviewed_by":null,"pool_validated_by":"Angelus","pool_committed_by":"Angelus"},{"action_type":"misc","pool":null,"roll":{"dice_string":"[3,1,2,9,0>3,1,2,6,2,0>0>9]","successes":5,"exceptional":true,"rolled_at":"2026-04-14T09:58:19.935Z","params":{"size":10,"again":10,"success":8,"exc":5,"rote":false}},"st_note":"","pool_player":"","pool_validated":"Intelligence 2 + Subterfuge 3 + Obfuscate 5 = 10","pool_status":"validated","notes_thread":[{"author_id":"405594065841946624","author_name":"Von Vagabond","text":"Safe Place now in Under Harbour","created_at":"2026-04-14T09:57:00.012Z"}],"story_context":"","resolved_at":null,"active_feed_specs":[],"pool_mod_spec":0,"nine_again":false,"rote":false,"eight_again":false},{"action_type":"misc","pool":null,"roll":null,"st_note":"","pool_player":"Msytery Cult Initiate 5","pool_validated":"","pool_status":"validated","notes_thread":[{"author_id":"405594065841946624","author_name":"Von Vagabond","text":"Its purring like a corrupt hat full of fucking deplorable arseholes. Tasty arseholes.","created_at":"2026-04-16T10:28:07.049Z"}],"story_context":"","resolved_at":null,"action_type_override":"maintenance","pool_validated_by":"Angelus"}],"merit_actions_resolved":[{"pool_player":"","pool_validated":"","pool_status":"resolved","notes_thread":[{"author_id":"405594065841946624","author_name":"Von Vagabond","text":"+1 Ambience","created_at":"2026-04-14T09:13:36.640Z"},{"author_id":"405594065841946624","author_name":"Von Vagabond","text":"More finance bros out late networking in bars after working the grind over time","created_at":"2026-04-15T22:21:20.044Z"}],"story_context":"","action_type_override":"ambience_increase"},{"pool_player":"","pool_validated":"","pool_status":"resolved","notes_thread":[{"author_id":"405594065841946624","author_name":"Von Vagabond","text":"+1 Ambience","created_at":"2026-04-14T09:13:49.863Z"},{"author_id":"405594065841946624","author_name":"Von Vagabond","text":"Late night trading is the talk of the town as the local members start loosening the grip on the nanny state.","created_at":"2026-04-15T22:21:57.620Z"}],"story_context":"","action_type_override":"ambience_increase"},{"pool_player":"","pool_validated":"","pool_status":"no_roll","notes_thread":[{"author_id":"405594065841946624","author_name":"Von Vagabond","text":"Work on a Necropolis has begun.","created_at":"2026-04-14T10:04:55.515Z"}],"story_context":"","action_type_override":"acquisition","st_response":"The cult works the politics and finance arms across the month and what it produces is infrastructural. A council environmental report that quietly rules a section of the Ultimo sewer loop unsafe for maintenance access. A contractor who is awarded a small job to run a concrete seal across a junction in the M11 tunnel works, recording it in the file as a construction accident. An archived rail easement that has been un-archived and then re-archived under a different filing so that the particular section beneath the Chinese Garden now belongs, administratively, to nowhere. The total effect is that substantial stretches of the subterranean city under the Harbour now exist only in your map. Work on a Necropolis has begun.","response_status":"draft","response_author":"a_morningstar"},{"pool_player":"","pool_validated":"","pool_status":"resolved","notes_thread":[{"author_id":"405594065841946624","author_name":"Von Vagabond","text":"They are calling the vigilante The Tracksuit Terror and he is targeting street crime, never enough to kill, but enough to make people seriously reconsider their career choices.","created_at":"2026-04-16T11:12:30.077Z"}],"story_context":"We are going to roll with this, but you should not in fact have received the information that is being followed up. Our mistake, ordinarily mortal contacts do not have the ability to pierce Obfuscate - so instead, some small detail in the information combined with a small detail of Ballsack's behaviour, and Yusuf intuited the connection.","action_type_override":"grow","merit_outcome":"approved"},{"pool_player":"","pool_validated":"","pool_status":"resolved","notes_thread":[{"author_id":"405594065841946624","author_name":"Von Vagabond","text":"You realise Yusuf, Xavier, and Reed are pretty much the only players in Financial Sphere. Though some mentions some guy that pays for information in the sector who someone by the description of Keeper.","created_at":"2026-04-16T11:16:03.357Z"}],"story_context":"","merit_outcome":"approved","st_response":"Your enquiry into the Finance sphere returns a picture that confirms what you suspected. The serious Kindred players in this space are you, Xavier, and Reed Justice. Three hands, and three hands only, operating at the level that matters. What catches your attention is a thread at the edges of the report. Somebody has been paying for information in the Finance sector across the month, at a Resources rating consistent with sustained Contact work. The description of the buyer is consistent with Keeper. He has not positioned himself as a Finance player. He has positioned himself as a man who wants to know what the Finance players are doing. File accordingly.","response_status":"draft","response_author":"a_morningstar"},{"pool_player":"","pool_validated":"","pool_status":"resolved","notes_thread":[{"author_id":"405594065841946624","author_name":"Von Vagabond","text":"Some firebrand named Rene has been throwing around some influence to make things a little worse for wear in the Harbour.","created_at":"2026-04-16T11:18:34.282Z"}],"story_context":"","merit_outcome":"approved","st_response":"Your Harbour-side contacts flag a pattern you had not been watching for. Somebody calling herself Rene, a Carthian firebrand by reputation, has been throwing influence around in ways calculated to make the Harbour a little worse for wear. Small drags against the larger lift, targeted in places that suggest she knows what she is doing. She is working against you and Reed and Wan and everyone else who has been lifting the territory. The amount of influence is not enormous. The deliberateness of it is.","response_status":"draft","response_author":"a_morningstar"}],"st_review":{"territory_overrides":{"1":"harbour","allies_0":"northshore","allies_1":"harbour","feeding":["harbour","northshore"]},"travel_discretion":"subtle","outcome_text":"## Letter from Home\n\nY,\n[E]ndless [Y]arns from th[E] [S]outh, I'll spare y[O]u.\n[N]othing new he[RE] worth the postage.\n[N]ew faces [E]verywhere, same old arguments.\n[HOLD] the line. Strange as ever.\n\n## Touchstone\n\nThe Turkish laundrette woman is folding sheets at the big table near the back when you come in, and she does not look up because she does not look up for anyone; the door chime is for her ears alone and she has long since stopped turning her head at it. You stand by the dryers pretending to wait for a load. You have stood here before. The fluorescent tube above the counter has been buzzing on the edge of failure for at least eight months. She has not replaced it because the light is still light.\nShe works the way she has always worked. A sheet lifted, shaken out, aligned corner to corner, halved, halved again, smoothed down the middle, stacked. The stack grows at her left hand. She does not hum. Her hands are older than you remember but they are the same hands, slow and exact, and the pink scar on the base of her thumb is still there from the burn she got on the steam press the summer before you left the district.\nA student comes in and asks about the machines, and she points at the sign without speaking, and he nods and goes to the machines, and she folds another sheet. You buy a small sachet of powder from the wall dispenser you do not need and leave coins on the counter. She does not count them. She never has. The door chimes behind you.\n\n## The Harbour\n\nThe Harbour is warming and the corners you crawl into are warming with it. The rough sleepers under the Anzac Bridge approaches and in the service recesses at Barangaroo are more numerous this month, the cold bringing them deeper into the places you work. Face in the crowd, you take what you need and leave a bottle and a blanket, and the blood comes up full, clean, the territory giving back. Reed Justice passes you on the Pyrmont footbridge and looks past you, which is the only acknowledgement that matters. What everyone is talking about is a clip on the nightly news of a carpark near the Pyrmont overpass. On two separate streets past midnight the regulars you know by sight are not where they usually sleep, bad dreams moving them along.\n\n## The North Shore\n\nThe Shore keeps its poor out of sight better than most territories, but the corners still hold. The rough sleepers behind St Leonards station, the ones in the loading docks at Artarmon, the ones nobody on Military Road admits are living two streets away. Face in the crowd, you take what you need and the blood comes up clean, a little shaded, a territory worked fairly. You pass Ivana Horvat near the North Sydney oval twice in the same week, both of you keeping to the fringes. At the back of an all-night pharmacy in Crows Nest a woman sees you before you have slipped, which is the month telling you someone has been paying attention.\n\n## Very Very Sneaky\n\nYou have been building Obfuscate into yourself across the whole cycle and by the end of the month the final layer settles. Oubliette goes onto the Siphon the night after you seal the lair. The space edits itself out of the under-Harbour's mental map the way a typographical error edits itself out of a document once the proofread is done. The tunnels approach it and do not arrive. The rats go around. The maintenance engineers who know this part of the system have already begun to misremember whether the chamber was ever there. You sleep better than you have slept in a century.\n\n## A fear cleanse of the Burrows\n\nYou walk the tunnels for three weeks and they give themselves up to you section by section. Maintenance overalls and a clipboard get you past the first two checkpoints. After that it is just you and Face in the Crowd and the dark, and the dark carries your work further than the work carries itself. The Cave Clan abandon their usual pitches in the first week. By the second the deeper settlements, the ones that have persisted since the Olympics, break up and move. You drift through the sleeping corners and let Nightmare do what Nightmare does. Grown men wake with their teeth chattering and run without being able to name what chased them. A woman curled beside a pipe dreams her way out into the street above before she is fully awake. By month's end the tunnels under Pyrmont, Balmain East, and the long loop beneath the Barangaroo foreshore and Hickson Road have emptied. The Burrows are yours to inhabit. Above ground the rough sleeper count has visibly risen, fresh bodies around the Anzac Bridge approaches and under the overpasses where there were none the week before. That is somebody else's problem. What you have built down here is a new kind of territory, unlit, unclaimed by any Regent, and waiting.\n\n## A rotten Nest\n\nThe Siphon is a large chamber and it is mostly empty when you start. You spend the first week moving your possessions down through the service tunnels, the coffin, the ledgers, the pieces that matter. The second week is the vitae work. You shed blood into the corners and the blood holds the shape you want it to hold; the space begins to exhale wrongness. You engineer the approaches so that anyone who comes down the wrong corridor hears distant screaming before they hear footsteps, and the screaming is not yours. By the third week the Burrows around your new lair behave themselves without you having to patrol them; the space has acquired a reputation the rats pass on to each other. By the end of the month you sleep here. Safe Place now in the Under-Harbour.\n\n## \"MMN Sees\"\n\nThe apparatus hums across the month. Networks maintained, new members grooming, resources allocated, the occasional small fire put out before it could become a large one. The North Shore arm in particular is in the best shape it has been in. A corrupt hat full of deplorable arseholes. Tasty arseholes. Xavier's arrival mid-cycle has tightened what you had already built in ways you might have resented from anyone else, and from Xavier you recognise as correction you needed.\n\n## Allies 3 (Finance)\n\nYour finance people have been leaning on the Mosman overtime culture all month. Late-night trading desk hours extended at two mid-tier firms, after-work drinks pushed past ten, a new cocktail bar behind Military Road that is drawing exactly the clientele you wanted. A contact sends you a photo of the bar's Tuesday crowd at 11pm. Suits on their third drink. The climb maketh the garden verdant.\n\n## Allies 2 (Politics)\n\nYour political people move a late-trading trial through a council subcommittee on the quiet. Three Pyrmont venues are now licensed past 2am for the duration of the pilot. A Herald business-section item the following week describes the loosening as a long-overdue modernisation. The 3am crowd arrives. The territory gets better for the kind of work you do and worse for everyone else, which is how you like it.\n\n## Contacts\n\nA piece of information you had not expected comes up through your networks. A vigilante has been working the criminal underside of the Dockyards across the month, beating the kind of street offender that deserves it, never to the point of killing, always to the point where the man will think seriously about his career choices. They are calling him the Tracksuit Terror. Your people have only surface-level detail, but something in the profile catches your attention for further follow-up.\n\nOOC ST  note: We are going to roll with this, but you should not in fact have received the information that is being followed up. Our mistake, ordinarily mortal contacts do not have the ability to pierce Obfuscate - so instead, some small detail in the information combined with a small detail of Ballsack's behaviour, and Yusuf intuited the connection.\n\n## Contacts\n\nYour contacts work the Finance angle on the Harbour question and come back with a picture that does not point where you expected it to. Nobody in the Finance sphere is working against the territory. The serious players here are you, Xavier, and Reed, and all three of you are pulling in the same direction. Whatever is dragging the Harbour down is not coming from the money side. Your contacts do flag one detail at the edge of the enquiry: somebody matching Keeper's description has been paying for information in the Finance sector across the month, not as a player but as a buyer of intelligence about the players. File that separately.\n\n## Contacts\n\nYour Harbour-side contacts flag a pattern you had not been watching for. Somebody calling herself Rene has been throwing influence around in ways calculated to make the Harbour a little worse for wear. Small drags against the larger lift, targeted in places that suggest she knows what she is doing. She is working against you and Reed and Wan and everyone else who has been lifting the territory. The amount of influence is not enormous. The deliberateness of it is.\n\n## Resources\n\nThe cult premises on the Shore receive a month's worth of investment that is designed to communicate rather than protect. New lighting, visible cameras that may or may not record, a front door that has been replaced with something heavier than a community hall requires. The interior is dressed with the quiet ostentation of money that wants to be noticed. There is no security. There does not need to be. The building looks like a trap, which is the point.\n\n## Skill Acquisition\n\nThree thermal cameras and two mesh monitors, encrypted, piezo-powered, the kind of equipment that does not appear in catalogues available to the public. Your police contact knows a man in the technical surveillance unit who has access to decommissioned stock. You meet him once in a carpark in Chatswood and the conversation is brief and one-directional. He leaves the equipment in the boot of a car that is not his. You collect it after he has gone. The cameras are installed on the cult premises within the week, covering every approach.\n\n## Mystery Cult Initiate\n\nThe cult works the politics and finance arms across the month and what it produces is infrastructural. A council environmental report that quietly rules a section of the Ultimo sewer loop unsafe for maintenance access. A contractor who is awarded a small job to run a concrete seal across a junction in the M11 tunnel works, recording it in the file as a construction accident. An archived rail easement that has been un-archived and then re-archived under a different filing so that the particular section beneath the Chinese Garden now belongs, administratively, to nowhere. The total effect is that substantial stretches of the subterranean city under the Harbour now exist only in your map. Work on a Necropolis has begun.\n\nTest","outcome_visibility":"published","published_at":"2026-04-17T08:16:45.334Z"},"st_narrative":{"letter_from_home":{"response":"Y,\n[E]ndless [Y]arns from th[E] [S]outh, I'll spare y[O]u.\n[N]othing new he[RE] worth the postage.\n[N]ew faces [E]verywhere, same old arguments.\n[HOLD] the line. Strange as ever.","author":"Angelus","status":"complete","revision_note":""},"touchstone":{"response":"The Turkish laundrette woman is folding sheets at the big table near the back when you come in, and she does not look up because she does not look up for anyone; the door chime is for her ears alone and she has long since stopped turning her head at it. You stand by the dryers pretending to wait for a load. You have stood here before. The fluorescent tube above the counter has been buzzing on the edge of failure for at least eight months. She has not replaced it because the light is still light.\nShe works the way she has always worked. A sheet lifted, shaken out, aligned corner to corner, halved, halved again, smoothed down the middle, stacked. The stack grows at her left hand. She does not hum. Her hands are older than you remember but they are the same hands, slow and exact, and the pink scar on the base of her thumb is still there from the burn she got on the steam press the summer before you left the district.\nA student comes in and asks about the machines, and she points at the sign without speaking, and he nods and goes to the machines, and she folds another sheet. You buy a small sachet of powder from the wall dispenser you do not need and leave coins on the counter. She does not count them. She never has. The door chimes behind you.","author":"Angelus","status":"complete","revision_note":""},"territory_reports":[{"territory_id":"harbour","response":"The Harbour is warming and the corners you crawl into are warming with it. The rough sleepers under the Anzac Bridge approaches and in the service recesses at Barangaroo are more numerous this month, the cold bringing them deeper into the places you work. Face in the crowd, you take what you need and leave a bottle and a blanket, and the blood comes up full, clean, the territory giving back. Reed Justice passes you on the Pyrmont footbridge and looks past you, which is the only acknowledgement that matters. What everyone is talking about is a clip on the nightly news of a carpark near the Pyrmont overpass. On two separate streets past midnight the regulars you know by sight are not where they usually sleep, bad dreams moving them along.","author":"Angelus","status":"complete","revision_note":""},{"territory_id":"northshore","response":"The Shore keeps its poor out of sight better than most territories, but the corners still hold. The rough sleepers behind St Leonards station, the ones in the loading docks at Artarmon, the ones nobody on Military Road admits are living two streets away. Face in the crowd, you take what you need and the blood comes up clean, a little shaded, a territory worked fairly. You pass Ivana Horvat near the North Sydney oval twice in the same week, both of you keeping to the fringes. At the back of an all-night pharmacy in Crows Nest a woman sees you before you have slipped, which is the month telling you someone has been paying attention.","author":"Angelus","status":"complete","revision_note":""}],"action_responses":[{"action_index":0,"response":"Your finance people have been leaning on the Mosman overtime culture all month. Late-night trading desk hours extended at two mid-tier firms, after-work drinks pushed past ten, a new cocktail bar behind Military Road that is drawing exactly the clientele you wanted. A contact sends you a photo of the bar's Tuesday crowd at 11pm. Suits on their third drink. The climb maketh the garden verdant.","author":"Angelus","status":"complete","revision_note":""},{"action_index":1,"response":"Your political people move a late-trading trial through a council subcommittee on the quiet. Three Pyrmont venues are now licensed past 2am for the duration of the pilot. A Herald business-section item the following week describes the loosening as a long-overdue modernisation. The 3am crowd arrives. The territory gets better for the kind of work you do and worse for everyone else, which is how you like it.\n","author":"Angelus","status":"complete","revision_note":""},{"action_index":2,"response":"The cult works the politics and finance arms across the month and what it produces is infrastructural. A council environmental report that quietly rules a section of the Ultimo sewer loop unsafe for maintenance access. A contractor who is awarded a small job to run a concrete seal across a junction in the M11 tunnel works, recording it in the file as a construction accident. An archived rail easement that has been un-archived and then re-archived under a different filing so that the particular section beneath the Chinese Garden now belongs, administratively, to nowhere. The total effect is that substantial stretches of the subterranean city under the Harbour now exist only in your map. Work on a Necropolis has begun.","author":"Angelus","status":"complete","revision_note":"This information in the wrong section"},{"action_index":3,"response":"A piece of information you had not expected comes up through your networks. A vigilante has been working the criminal underside of the Dockyards across the month, beating the kind of street offender that deserves it, never to the point of killing, always to the point where the man will think seriously about his career choices. They are calling him the Tracksuit Terror. Your people have only surface-level detail, but something in the profile catches your attention for further follow-up.\n\nOOC ST  note: We are going to roll with this, but you should not in fact have received the information that is being followed up. Our mistake, ordinarily mortal contacts do not have the ability to pierce Obfuscate - so instead, some small detail in the information combined with a small detail of Ballsack's behaviour, and Yusuf intuited the connection.","author":"Angelus","status":"complete","revision_note":""},{"action_index":4,"response":"Your contacts work the Finance angle on the Harbour question and come back with a picture that does not point where you expected it to. Nobody in the Finance sphere is working against the territory. The serious players here are you, Xavier, and Reed, and all three of you are pulling in the same direction. Whatever is dragging the Harbour down is not coming from the money side. Your contacts do flag one detail at the edge of the enquiry: somebody matching Keeper's description has been paying for information in the Finance sector across the month, not as a player but as a buyer of intelligence about the players. File that separately.","author":"Angelus","status":"complete","revision_note":"This output in in the wrong section"},{"action_index":5,"response":"Your Harbour-side contacts flag a pattern you had not been watching for. Somebody calling herself Rene has been throwing influence around in ways calculated to make the Harbour a little worse for wear. Small drags against the larger lift, targeted in places that suggest she knows what she is doing. She is working against you and Reed and Wan and everyone else who has been lifting the territory. The amount of influence is not enormous. The deliberateness of it is.","author":"Angelus","status":"complete","revision_note":"This output is in the wrong section"},{"action_index":6,"response":"The cult premises on the Shore receive a month's worth of investment that is designed to communicate rather than protect. New lighting, visible cameras that may or may not record, a front door that has been replaced with something heavier than a community hall requires. The interior is dressed with the quiet ostentation of money that wants to be noticed. There is no security. There does not need to be. The building looks like a trap, which is the point.","author":"Angelus","status":"complete","revision_note":""},{"action_index":7,"response":"Three thermal cameras and two mesh monitors, encrypted, piezo-powered, the kind of equipment that does not appear in catalogues available to the public. Your police contact knows a man in the technical surveillance unit who has access to decommissioned stock. You meet him once in a carpark in Chatswood and the conversation is brief and one-directional. He leaves the equipment in the boot of a car that is not his. You collect it after he has gone. The cameras are installed on the cult premises within the week, covering every approach.","author":"Angelus","status":"complete","revision_note":""}],"project_responses":[{"project_index":0,"response":"You have been building Obfuscate into yourself across the whole cycle and by the end of the month the final layer settles. Oubliette goes onto the Siphon the night after you seal the lair. The space edits itself out of the under-Harbour's mental map the way a typographical error edits itself out of a document once the proofread is done. The tunnels approach it and do not arrive. The rats go around. The maintenance engineers who know this part of the system have already begun to misremember whether the chamber was ever there. You sleep better than you have slept in a century.","author":"Angelus","status":"complete","revision_note":""},{"project_index":1,"response":"You walk the tunnels for three weeks and they give themselves up to you section by section. Maintenance overalls and a clipboard get you past the first two checkpoints. After that it is just you and Face in the Crowd and the dark, and the dark carries your work further than the work carries itself. The Cave Clan abandon their usual pitches in the first week. By the second the deeper settlements, the ones that have persisted since the Olympics, break up and move. You drift through the sleeping corners and let Nightmare do what Nightmare does. Grown men wake with their teeth chattering and run without being able to name what chased them. A woman curled beside a pipe dreams her way out into the street above before she is fully awake. By month's end the tunnels under Pyrmont, Balmain East, and the long loop beneath the Barangaroo foreshore and Hickson Road have emptied. The Burrows are yours to inhabit. Above ground the rough sleeper count has visibly risen, fresh bodies around the Anzac Bridge approaches and under the overpasses where there were none the week before. That is somebody else's problem. What you have built down here is a new kind of territory, unlit, unclaimed by any Regent, and waiting.","author":"Angelus","status":"complete","revision_note":""},{"project_index":2,"response":"The Siphon is a large chamber and it is mostly empty when you start. You spend the first week moving your possessions down through the service tunnels, the coffin, the ledgers, the pieces that matter. The second week is the vitae work. You shed blood into the corners and the blood holds the shape you want it to hold; the space begins to exhale wrongness. You engineer the approaches so that anyone who comes down the wrong corridor hears distant screaming before they hear footsteps, and the screaming is not yours. By the third week the Burrows around your new lair behave themselves without you having to patrol them; the space has acquired a reputation the rats pass on to each other. By the end of the month you sleep here. Safe Place now in the Under-Harbour.","author":"Angelus","status":"complete","revision_note":""},{"project_index":3,"response":"The apparatus hums across the month. Networks maintained, new members grooming, resources allocated, the occasional small fire put out before it could become a large one. The North Shore arm in particular is in the best shape it has been in. A corrupt hat full of deplorable arseholes. Tasty arseholes. Xavier's arrival mid-cycle has tightened what you had already built in ways you might have resented from anyone else, and from Xavier you recognise as correction you needed.","author":"Angelus","status":"complete","revision_note":""}],"general_notes":"Test","locked":true,"resource_approvals":[null,null,null,null,null,null,{"action_index":6,"approved":true,"flag_note":"","reviewed_by":"Angelus"}]},"acquisitions_resolved":[{"pool_player":"","pool_validated":"","pool_status":"validated","notes_thread":[{"author_id":"405594065841946624","author_name":"Von Vagabond","text":"If people investigate the area it will look like a Safe Place +3","created_at":"2026-04-16T11:35:54.850Z"}],"story_context":"If people investigate the area it will look like a Safe Place +3","pool_validated_by":"Von Vagabond"},{"pool_player":"","pool_validated":"","pool_status":"validated","notes_thread":[],"story_context":"I'm sure the real-world tech is very cool; but can you please let us know what piece of equipment from one of the books you want (Chronical of Darkness or Hurt Locker) or it will just be a very nice camera.","pool_validated_by":"Von Vagabond"}],"feeding_roll_player":{"cols":[{"r":{"v":5,"s":false,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":8,"s":true,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":2,"s":false,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":8,"s":true,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":8,"s":true,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":5,"s":false,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":1,"s":false,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":2,"s":false,"x":false},"ch":[]},{"r":{"v":4,"s":false,"x":false},"ch":[]}],"successes":3,"vessels":3,"safeVitae":6,"methodName":"Other","pool":9,"again":9,"breakdown":"ST confirmed: Presence 4 + Empathy 4 = 8 + Motives +1 — 9-Again","rolledAt":"2026-04-17T08:11:49.869Z","dramaticFailure":false},"feeding_deferred":null,"feeding_vitae_allocation":[2,2,2],"feeding_vitae_tally":{"herd":5,"ambience":3,"ambience_territory":"North Shore","oath_of_fealty":0,"ghouls":0,"rite_cost":0,"manual":0,"total_bonus":8}},{"_id":"69da37d0cc5483a3c77027a1","chapter_id":"69d0a3c5052b57f6be774e69","character_id":"69d73ea49162ece35897a47c","character_name":"Alice Vunder","player_name":"Katherine Honan","status":"submitted","timestamp":"9/04/2026 0:43","attended":true,"_raw":{"submission":{"timestamp":"9/04/2026 0:43","email":"honankatherine@gmail.com","player_name":"Katherine Honan","character_name":"Alice Vunder","attended_last_game":true},"narrative":{"travel_description":"I can't remember the entire answer I wrote but it involved getting lost a lot. It was something like taking the wrong train and getting off at the wrong station and having to catch a train back to where I was meant to go and then still getting lost","game_recount":"Helped Anichka with braiding her red ribbons. They made her think of red ribbons of blood in the water.\nSaw a fight at the club when went dancing with cyrus. Instantly went to help Kindred and keep the masquerade intact.\nTried to bargain with Conrad for regency but he just insulted all crones, then afterwards said he was only trying to shield another territory and offered a boon to Alice. She accepted it.\nBecame regent without much warning\nChatted with Renee about how keeper can mess with memories, then realised alice doesn't remember bits from the party with cyrus","standout_rp":"Conrad, for being a religious shit. Anichka, for helping Alice realise that she is struggling with the anger of the beast.","ic_correspondence":"I had an email alice sent to her family that was about the new club and how she is now in a new position and feels very nervous about it and also that all these people at the new club talking about bringing in the old ways and the old people made her feel protective of her home country","most_trusted_pc":"anichka, brandy, tegan, maybe cryus","actively_harming_pc":"Conrad. but not in a way where alice would endanger herself or get caught.","aspirations":"same as before"},"regency":{"is_regent":true,"territory":"The North Shore","residency_grants":["Alice Vunder","Preacher Willows","Brandy LaRoux","Yusuf the Carthian","Balls the Invictus"],"total_residency_count":5,"regency_action":"This is not a place to bring the old world to and impose old ways upon. This territory is its own entity, and must be respected as such."},"feeding":{"method":"Primary Feeding Pool: Intelligence + Stealth \nBlood Type: Human\nFeeding Style: Hangs out near the Ivy club and feeds on a guy trying to pressure a far too drunk girl to go home with him.","territories":{"The Academy":"Not feeding here","The Harbour":"Not feeding here","The Dockyards":"Not feeding here","The Second City":"Not feeding here","The North Shore":"Resident","The Barrens (No Territory)":"Not feeding here"}},"influence":{"The Academy":0,"The Harbour":0,"The Dockyards":0,"The Second City":0,"The Shore":1},"projects":[{"action_type":"patrol_scout","action_type_raw":"Patrol/Scout: Attempt to monitor a given Territory or area 👀","primary_pool":{"expression":"Presence 3 + Socialise 2 + Contact street 3 = 8","size":8},"secondary_pool":{"expression":"NA","size":null},"desired_outcome":"Keep the Shore safe","description":"Project Name: Keeping it Tight! (Alice version, credit to Jack)\nCharacters Involved: Me (and Preacher Willows (Leo T), Brandy LaRoux (Ash), Ivana Horvat (Lyn H), Balls the Invictus)\nMerits & Bonuses:\nXp Spend: n/a\nProject Description: \nThe Shore is actively patrolled to keep out poachers or interlopers, and to reinforce the Masquerade with the Great Unwashed. Let it be known by all that Court has been established, and a Regent chosen for this district who watches from every shadow. Kindred may pass through, quickly and without stopping -- but pause for too long at your peril!","project_name":"Keeping it Tight! (Alice version, credit to Jack)","characters":null,"xp_spend":"n/a","merits":null,"bonuses":null,"detail":"Characters Involved: Me (and Preacher Willows (Leo T), Brandy LaRoux (Ash), Ivana Horvat (Lyn H), Balls the Invictus)\nMerits & Bonuses:\nProject Description: \nThe Shore is actively patrolled to keep out poachers or interlopers, and to reinforce the Masquerade with the Great Unwashed. Let it be known by all that Court has been established, and a Regent chosen for this district who watches from every s